course: dictionary
lesson: 6797
title: Ordinary and out of the ordinary
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ordinary means normal, usual or plain: not special or different. Think of an ordinary day, when you wake up, eat breakfast and go to school. «Juries of ordinary people, usually twelve, grew in England.» Here ordinary people are everyday people, not kings or judges.
explain: Ordinary can also appear in the phrase «out of the ordinary», which means unusual or surprising. If a teacher says «Nothing out of the ordinary happened on the trip», she means nothing strange or surprising happened. Ask yourself: is the sentence saying something is normal, or saying something is special?
explain: Context helps you work out which meaning is right. «A miracle is an amazing event beyond the ordinary» tells you that a miracle is more than normal, because amazing and beyond are the clue words. Read the words around the word, swap in your meaning, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Ordinary means normal, usual or plain.
fact: «Out of the ordinary» means unusual or surprising.
fact: «An ordinary day» is a day with nothing special in it.
fact: «Ordinary people» means everyday people, not special or famous people.
fact: «Out of the ordinary» works like a noun phrase, as in «nothing out of the ordinary».
exercise: «Juries of ordinary people grew in England.» What does ordinary mean here? | People who work as judges | *Normal, everyday people | Very rich and famous people | Strange, unusual people
exercise: A teacher says, «Nothing out of the ordinary happened on the trip.» What does this mean? | The trip was very long | *Nothing unusual or surprising happened | The teacher lost her bag | Something amazing happened every minute
exercise: Which day is an ordinary day? | A day when a dragon lands in the playground | A day with snow in July | A day when the sun shines at midnight | *A day of breakfast, school and tea
test: In «a miracle is an amazing event beyond the ordinary», what is the ordinary? | Events that are hidden | Sad events | Amazing events | *Normal, everyday events
test: Which word is closest in meaning to ordinary? | Shiny | *Normal | Loud | Strange
exam: Ayo says «out of the ordinary» just means ordinary. Why is he wrong? | It is a type of food | It means exactly normal | It means very quiet | *It means unusual or surprising
